          "id": "spooktacular-science-day-2026-10-24",
          "title": "Spooktacular Science Day",
          "description": "A family Halloween celebration at The Franklin Institute blending science with seasonal fun, 11:00 am to 3:00 pm. Highlights include a museum-wide trick-or-treat through themed doors (bring your own bag), a costume parade down the Atrium ramp, squid dissection, a pumpkin-carving demonstration, the Electricity Show, and hands-on activities including Shrinky Dinks, Pepper's Ghost, and Jacob's Ladder. Costumes encouraged; suited to families and kids of all ages. Free with general admission.",
