          "id": "stories-of-science-craft-tober-2026-10-10",
          "title": "Stories of Science: Craft-tober",
          "description": "A free family-friendly Saturday program at the Science History Institute, 10am to 5pm, highlighting surprising and spellbinding stories from the history of science. October's theme is Nobel Prize Week: guests can pick up trivia about the prizes and decorate a medal to keep. Also offered are an Object Explorer touch table, scavenger hunts at several difficulty levels, conversations with Gallery Guides, and a Kid's Corner with puzzles, building toys, and science-themed children's books. Admission is free and reservations are not required.",
